512
00:36:05,371 --> 00:36:07,706
Don't say what you're about to say.

513
00:36:18,676 --> 00:36:20,135
ONE MONTH LEFT UNTIL THE CSAT
YOU'VE GOT THIS!

514
00:36:30,354 --> 00:36:32,856
The fruit-and-cream cake.

515
00:36:32,940 --> 00:36:34,066
I'll take this one.

516
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:50,791
What do you mean? We signed
a lump-sum deposit for this place.

517
00:36:50,874 --> 00:36:52,209
How many times do I have to tell you?

518
00:36:52,292 --> 00:36:55,879
Your father took out
the original deposit

519
00:36:55,963 --> 00:36:57,923
and switched to monthly rent
ages ago.

520
00:36:58,006 --> 00:37:01,385
And now he's taken what was left
of the security deposit.

521
00:37:01,468 --> 00:37:03,971
- It was switched to monthly...
- Jeez.

522
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:11,520
I asked you not to tell my sister.

523
00:37:11,937 --> 00:37:13,355
What are you talking about?

524
00:37:13,439 --> 00:37:14,857
It's exactly what you heard.

525
00:37:16,275 --> 00:37:17,651
I've been paying the rent.

526
00:37:17,943 --> 00:37:18,944
What?

527
00:37:19,486 --> 00:37:20,487
With what money...

528
00:37:20,571 --> 00:37:23,282
I'm sick and tired
of dealing with this!

529
00:37:23,365 --> 00:37:26,201
Just pack up and leave, okay?
I want you gone.

530
00:37:26,618 --> 00:37:27,828
Is that what you're after?

531
00:37:28,662 --> 00:37:30,330
You wanted us gone

532
00:37:30,414 --> 00:37:33,292
so you went behind my back
and gave the deposit to him.

533
00:37:33,375 --> 00:37:34,793
Now you're kicking us to the curb.

534
00:37:36,170 --> 00:37:37,463
All while taking my rent money.

535
00:37:37,546 --> 00:37:38,922
Come on.

536
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:43,510
The lease is
in your father's name, anyway.

537
00:37:45,179 --> 00:37:48,265
You didn't say a word
when I sent you rent every month.

538
00:37:48,348 --> 00:37:49,475
Oh, for goodness' sake!

539
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:54,021
I don't want trouble in my building
over a measly sum, okay?

540
00:37:54,313 --> 00:37:57,065
One day, your dad is here
throwing a fit.

541
00:37:57,149 --> 00:37:59,526
The next day, I've got thugs
roaming the halls.

542
00:37:59,610 --> 00:38:01,487
And look at this mess right now!

543
00:38:03,238 --> 00:38:06,408
My tenants are filing complaints
left and right.

544
00:38:06,492 --> 00:38:08,577
So you deliberately returned
the deposit

545
00:38:08,952 --> 00:38:10,496
to force us out.

546
00:38:13,248 --> 00:38:15,501
I'll wire you the security deposit.

547
00:38:16,460 --> 00:38:17,753
It's 8 million won, right?

548
00:38:18,086 --> 00:38:20,464
- Geon-tae.
- Well...

549
00:38:29,681 --> 00:38:31,517
CHECKING ACCOUNT
BALANCE: 0 WON

550
00:38:36,063 --> 00:38:38,607
OKI CAPITAL

551
00:38:38,690 --> 00:38:40,442
WITHDRAWN MONEY: 5,702,830 WON

552
00:38:42,778 --> 00:38:43,904
Well...

553
00:38:53,789 --> 00:38:56,792
<i>The number you have dialed is</i>
<i>currently unavailable.</i>

554
00:38:56,875 --> 00:38:58,794
<i>Please try again later.</i>

555
00:38:59,837 --> 00:39:01,338
Looks like there's a problem.

556
00:39:04,383 --> 00:39:05,634
NEW MESSAGE

557
00:39:07,761 --> 00:39:09,263
IGNORING MY MESSAGES?
SEND ME MONEY

558
00:39:09,346 --> 00:39:10,514
HOW MUCH IS THE SCHOLARSHIP?

559
00:39:10,597 --> 00:39:12,891
SORRY, SON
I'LL PAY YOU BACK SOON

560
00:39:19,439 --> 00:39:21,984
Give me just three days.

561
00:39:22,276 --> 00:39:24,319
- What are you saying?
- Then 10 million won.

562
00:39:25,529 --> 00:39:27,030
I'm raising it to 10 million.

563
00:39:27,114 --> 00:39:28,740
The previous sum doesn't meet
the market rate.

564
00:39:28,824 --> 00:39:32,452
Every two-bedroom place around here
has charged 10 million for years.

565
00:39:32,786 --> 00:39:34,496
I'll wire it to you in three days.

566
00:39:34,913 --> 00:39:36,081
Leave for today.

567
00:39:36,832 --> 00:39:37,875
And if you don't?

568
00:39:38,208 --> 00:39:39,585
You'll pack up and leave then.

569
00:39:39,668 --> 00:39:41,086
No excuses, okay?

570
00:39:42,921 --> 00:39:44,006
Goodness.

571
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:46,967
You think I enjoy doing this?

572
00:39:47,843 --> 00:39:50,387
Jeez, look at how messy
this place is.

573
00:39:50,470 --> 00:39:52,014
It gives me a headache.

574
00:39:53,223 --> 00:39:54,266
Goodness.

575
00:39:55,809 --> 00:39:57,185
What money could you possibly have?

576
00:39:57,269 --> 00:40:00,147
- My scholarship.
- Just how big is this scholarship?

577
00:40:00,230 --> 00:40:02,482
Big enough to cover half
of our living expenses and the rent?

578
00:40:03,901 --> 00:40:05,485
Do you think I'm an idiot?

579
00:40:05,819 --> 00:40:07,195
This makes no sense.

580
00:40:07,279 --> 00:40:09,656
How could you not tell me
we'd switched to monthly rent?

581
00:40:10,032 --> 00:40:11,575
Because I knew how you'd react.

582
00:40:12,409 --> 00:40:13,452
What?

583
00:40:15,621 --> 00:40:18,373
Because I knew
you'd play the martyr again.

584
00:40:18,457 --> 00:40:19,625
If you'd known

585
00:40:19,875 --> 00:40:21,084
you would've quit the academy again

586
00:40:21,168 --> 00:40:24,212
and picked up more part-time jobs
to pay the rent alone.

587
00:40:24,504 --> 00:40:25,547
Am I wrong?

588
00:40:26,381 --> 00:40:29,301
Who's the adult around here?

589
00:40:29,843 --> 00:40:31,094
I am, so I should be working.

590
00:40:31,345 --> 00:40:32,888
You're a student too.

591
00:40:32,971 --> 00:40:35,307
How will you find a job
and save up enough for a deposit?

592
00:40:35,390 --> 00:40:36,975
You're scraping by on minimum wage.

593
00:40:38,393 --> 00:40:40,187
- You...
- Would you feel better

594
00:40:40,938 --> 00:40:42,147
if we both ended up homeless?

595
00:40:47,861 --> 00:40:49,196
I have some money saved up.

596
00:40:49,488 --> 00:40:50,572
About 3 million won.

597
00:40:52,574 --> 00:40:54,242
I know it's not much.

598
00:40:54,660 --> 00:40:56,161
We'll give that
to the landlady first.

599
00:40:57,496 --> 00:40:59,790
My academy classes
are fully funded, anyway.

600
00:40:59,873 --> 00:41:02,125
- If I quit and work full-time...
- Stop!

601
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:06,588
Why is giving up so easy for you?

602
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:08,757
Don't you care
about all the work you've put in?

603
00:41:08,840 --> 00:41:11,051
If someone told me
to throw my studies away right now

604
00:41:11,134 --> 00:41:12,678
I'd go insane.

605
00:41:13,303 --> 00:41:14,972
How can you say it so easily?

606
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:18,517
Don't you have any desire
to escape this miserable life?

607
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,519
Has it ever occurred to you

608
00:41:20,602 --> 00:41:23,146
that we're still stuck in this mess
because you always act like this?

609
00:41:24,982 --> 00:41:27,609
This is the most important time
of your life.

610
00:41:27,693 --> 00:41:30,028
It's not just me!
I told you, I have the money!

611
00:41:30,112 --> 00:41:31,279
I have the money

612
00:41:31,363 --> 00:41:35,075
so neither of us
has to sacrifice anything!

613
00:41:43,333 --> 00:41:44,376
Please.

614
00:41:48,505 --> 00:41:50,382
Stop saying you'll give up

615
00:41:50,716 --> 00:41:52,259
and sacrifice yourself for me.

616
00:41:53,427 --> 00:41:55,012
Every time I hear it...

617
00:41:57,389 --> 00:41:58,849
I feel like I can't breathe.

618
00:42:37,387 --> 00:42:38,930
ACADEMIC EXCELLENCE SCHOLARSHIP

619
00:43:19,930 --> 00:43:21,264
You know the drill, right?

620
00:43:21,348 --> 00:43:23,350
Of course. I make sure to tell her

621
00:43:23,433 --> 00:43:24,935
that her tuition's covered
by the scholarship.

622
00:43:26,603 --> 00:43:27,646
Thank you.

623
00:43:28,105 --> 00:43:30,315
I'm so curious, though.

624
00:43:31,108 --> 00:43:33,068
What's your relationship?
Are you her boyfriend?

625
00:43:36,947 --> 00:43:40,450
TOP POLICE ACADEMY

626
00:43:43,286 --> 00:43:45,539
I-yeon might say she wants to quit.

627
00:43:45,622 --> 00:43:47,582
If she does, tell her
she can't quit in the middle

628
00:43:47,666 --> 00:43:49,626
because she already received
the scholarship.

629
00:44:03,306 --> 00:44:06,434
I-YEON'S BIRTHDAY

630
00:44:15,026 --> 00:44:16,069
DIALING
H

631
00:44:25,912 --> 00:44:27,455
INCOMING CALL
K

632
00:44:30,292 --> 00:44:31,585
<i>Give me a job the day after tomorrow.</i>

633
00:44:33,170 --> 00:44:34,337
What?

634
00:44:34,421 --> 00:44:37,507
You quit, ghosted me for a month,
and now you call me?

635
00:44:37,591 --> 00:44:39,467
So you want me to back out?

636
00:44:39,759 --> 00:44:42,596
<i>- You don't need me?</i>
- That's right! I don't need you.

637
00:44:43,305 --> 00:44:44,514
<i>You little bastard.</i>

638
00:44:45,682 --> 00:44:47,309
You shouldn't treat me like this.

639
00:44:47,392 --> 00:44:49,895
<i>Sometimes, you seem to forget</i>
<i>what I have on you.</i>

640
00:44:51,104 --> 00:44:53,773
<i>Get everything ready so I can take</i>
<i>the exam in two days.</i>

641
00:44:55,275 --> 00:44:57,194
And I want an advance,
including next month's pay.

642
00:45:03,074 --> 00:45:04,075
Bye.

643
00:45:12,751 --> 00:45:15,003
I can't even do anything
about this kid.

644
00:45:15,086 --> 00:45:16,171
IDENTIFICATION CARD

645
00:45:18,006 --> 00:45:19,299
KANG GEON-TAE

646
00:45:29,059 --> 00:45:31,061
ADMISSIONS TICKET
CHOI HYUN-BIN

647
00:45:31,144 --> 00:45:33,980
IDENTIFICATION CARD
CHOI HYUN-BIN

648
00:47:04,279 --> 00:47:05,322
DIALING
H

649
00:47:07,699 --> 00:47:10,785
<i>The number you have dialed is</i>
<i>currently unavailable.</i>

650
00:47:10,869 --> 00:47:12,620
<i>Please try again later.</i>

651
00:47:14,706 --> 00:47:17,292
<i>Sorry, something came up.</i>
<i>I can't talk on the phone.</i>

652
00:47:21,212 --> 00:47:22,422
<i>I need the cash now.</i>

653
00:47:25,383 --> 00:47:27,093
<i>I'm on a business trip.</i>
<i>I can wire it.</i>

654
00:47:29,888 --> 00:47:31,264
<i>I don't want a paper trail.</i>

655
00:47:33,266 --> 00:47:34,601
<i>The morning after tomorrow.</i>

656
00:47:34,684 --> 00:47:36,394
<i>At the crosswalk</i>
<i>just past the intersection.</i>

657
00:47:43,234 --> 00:47:44,778
TUTORING PAYMENT DATE

658
00:47:44,861 --> 00:47:46,696
OCTOBER MOCK EXAM

659
00:47:51,534 --> 00:47:52,994
HOURLY WAGE 10,100 WON

660
00:47:53,078 --> 00:47:54,371
GANGMUN GROCERY MARKET

661
00:47:54,913 --> 00:47:56,790
<i>You're scraping by on minimum wage.</i>

662
00:47:56,873 --> 00:47:58,458
You're a student too.

663
00:47:58,792 --> 00:48:01,211
How will you find a job
and save up enough for a deposit?

664
00:48:04,297 --> 00:48:06,132
SORT BY HIGHEST PAY

665
00:48:06,216 --> 00:48:07,717
PLUS NEXT BAR
HOURLY WAGE 100,000 WON

666
00:48:11,971 --> 00:48:13,264
KING BAR
PREMIUM WORK ENVIRONMENT

667
00:48:13,348 --> 00:48:15,141
HOURLY WAGE 85,000 WON

668
00:48:22,190 --> 00:48:23,316
<i>JANG JEONG-HUN'S</i>
<i>POLICE SCIENCE TEXTBOOK</i>

669
00:48:23,400 --> 00:48:25,735
Let's pick up
where we left off last class.

670
00:48:26,069 --> 00:48:29,239
It's the fundamental ideology
and values of the police force.

671
00:49:13,074 --> 00:49:14,117
Mr. Han Jung-do?

672
00:49:36,973 --> 00:49:39,476
Han Jung-do, you're under arrest

673
00:49:39,559 --> 00:49:41,603
on charges including
forgery of official documents.

674
00:49:41,686 --> 00:49:44,439
You have the right to an attorney,
the right to defend yourself

675
00:49:44,522 --> 00:49:46,649
the right to challenge your arrest
and the right to remain silent.

676
00:49:46,733 --> 00:49:49,068
Do you have a warrant?
What division are you from?

677
00:49:49,152 --> 00:49:50,945
This is police brutality!

678
00:49:53,573 --> 00:49:55,033
Get off!

679
00:49:55,116 --> 00:49:56,910
What the... Hold on.

680
00:50:13,426 --> 00:50:14,886
Let go!

681
00:50:46,042 --> 00:50:47,252
<i>Don't look back.</i>

682
00:50:48,586 --> 00:50:49,879
<i>Don't do it.</i>

683
00:50:51,923 --> 00:50:55,176
<i>Don't you ever look back.</i>

684
00:53:48,558 --> 00:53:50,518
Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
